<article class="env-lemma" id="0B6Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B6Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0B6Q">48.8.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of Noetherian schemes. Let $V \subset Y$ be an open such that $f^{-1}(V) \to V$ is an isomorphism. Then for $K \in D_\mathit{QCoh}^+(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ the map (<a href="/tag/0A9S" data-tag="0A9S">48.8.0.1</a>) restricts to an isomorphism over $f^{-1}(V)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0A9P" data-tag="0A9P">48.4.4</a> the map (<a href="/tag/0A9L" data-tag="0A9L">48.4.1.1</a>) is an isomorphism for objects of $D_\mathit{QCoh}^+(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. Hence Lemma <a href="/tag/0B6P" data-tag="0B6P">48.8.2</a> tells us the restriction of (<a href="/tag/0A9S" data-tag="0A9S">48.8.0.1</a>) for $K$ to $f^{-1}(V)$ is the map (<a href="/tag/0A9S" data-tag="0A9S">48.8.0.1</a>) for $K|_ V$ and $f^{-1}(V) \to V$. Thus it suffices to show that the map is an isomorphism when $f$ is the identity morphism. This is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>